{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CfQiyPsTjcwxpAGSpoURk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013RGdUQAkm5k8VwJKSpHfUg","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python - <<'EOF'\np='learning/formula_search.py'; s=open(p).read()\ns = s.replace('''2. **PySR** (soft import; `pip install pysr`, which bootstraps Julia on first\n   use) with the same operators plus `sqrt`, `square` and `log`, on a held-out\n   fifth of the files, so its Pareto front can be read beside the enumerated\n   winner and the boosting baseline on the same rows.''',\n'''2. **PySR** (soft import; `pip install pysr`, which bootstraps Julia on first\n   use) with the same operators plus `sqrt`, `square` and `log`, on a held-out\n   fifth of the files, so its Pareto front can be read beside the enumerated\n   winner and the boosting baseline on the same rows. Each PySR fit runs in a\n   child process (`--pysr-child`, internal): Julia's garbage collector aborts\n   a process that has forked a `multiprocessing` pool, which the enumerated\n   search does, and a child that dies costs one row rather than the run.\n   The tables above it are written to `--out` before PySR starts.''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\n\np='learning/requirements.txt'; s=open(p).read()\ns += '''# Optional, behind a soft import in learning/formula_search.py: symbolic\n# regression (bootstraps Julia on first use). Without it the enumerated search\n# runs alone and the PySR section of the tables says so.\npysr\n'''\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\n\np='tests/test_formula_search.py'; s=open(p).read()\ns = s.replace('''    pair_search,\n    search,\n)''', '''    pair_search,\n    pysr_front,\n    search,\n)''')\ns += '''\n\ndef test_pysr_child_failure_is_an_exception_not_a_crash(tmp_path):\n    # The child is a separate interpreter; here it is given a target it cannot\n    # fit (a single row, so PySR would refuse) and must come back as an error\n    # the study can record as one failed row. Runs without pysr installed\n    # too: the child fails at import or at fit, either way through the same\n    # RuntimeError, and nothing else in the process is touched.\n    X = np.array([[1.0, 2.0]])\n    y = np.array([3.0])\n    with pytest.raises(RuntimeError, match=\"PySR child exited\"):\n        pysr_front(X, y, X, [\"a\", \"b\"], seconds=1, threads=1)\n'''\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ntimeout 300 python -m pytest tests/test_formula_search.py -q -k pysr_child 2>&1 | tail -3","description":"Update docstring, requirements and add a child-failure test","timeout":300000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":494,"cache_read_input_tokens":100665,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":494,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"12577c41-7101-4638-b007-8765a211c262","uuid":"f1722a09-c35a-4e09-803f-3c4df82597cf","timestamp":"2026-09-25T19:39:52.227Z","request_id":"req_011CfQiyPCnDvcm8jnSTZD2j","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_013RGdUQAkm5k8VwJKSpHfUg":{"command":"cd /home/al/dev/MOSP && python - <<'EOF'\np='learning/formula_search.py'; s=open(p).read()\ns = s.replace('''2. **PySR** (soft import; `pip install pysr`, which bootstraps Julia on first\n   use) with the same operators plus `sqrt`, `square` and `log`, on a held-out\n   fifth of the files, so its Pareto front can be read beside the enumerated\n   winner and the boosting baseline on the same rows.''',\n'''2. **PySR** (soft import; `pip install pysr`, which bootstraps Julia on first\n   use) with the same operators plus `sqrt`, `square` and `log`, on a held-out\n   fifth of the files, so its Pareto front can be read beside the enumerated\n   winner and the boosting baseline on the same rows. Each PySR fit r