{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CfQnK9MW7AWqFztJoJXcn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Item 05 is done. The full suite passes (750 passed, 2 skipped, 1 xfailed, 77 s), no study or PySR processes remain, the recertify run still has its 12 processes, and nothing was written to `solutions/` or any solver file.\n\n**What this iteration delivered**\n\n- `learning/formula_search.py`, finished from iteration 5's committed module: enumerated monomial and pair search with least-absolute-deviation constants, nested protocol, LightGBM baseline, PySR on a held-out fifth of the files, and a new sandwich table with hand-fixed constants. Full run takes about 400 s on 16 workers and writes `reports/formula_tables.md`.\n- PySR was the reason iteration 5 never produced tables. Julia's garbage collector crashed on six of seven fits at 16 threads and 10,000 iterations, in-process or in a fresh child, with or without hitting the wall-clock stop. Each fit now runs in a child process with one retry at 4 threads and 2,000 iterations, which finished every time, and the enumerated tables are flushed to disk before PySR starts.\n- Three new tests (13 total in the module): the sandwich table on a four-row hand-computed frame, a planted bound violation, and the child's failure path. `pysr` is now an optional entry in `learning/requirements.txt`.\n- Section 5 appended to `reports/ml_nature.md`; PROGRESS.md gained the Iteration 7 entry and now reads 5/8 solved; item 05 is marked done.\n\n**Findings, in brief**\n\n- No clean formula for the residual. The best closed form scores grouped MAE 0.303 against 0.431 for the constant zero and 0.260 for LightGBM. Its variable is degree dispersion times separator size, and on every degree-regular graph in the corpus the gap is zero, but those are complete graphs, unions of cycles and one Miller graph, so no conjecture is stated.\n- The optimum does have a clean formula, and both searches agree on it. With treewidth heuristics allowed it is `tw_min_fill + 1`. From structure alone it is `1 + sqrt(degeneracy · RCM bandwidth)`, constants exactly 1 and 1, chosen in all five outer folds and by PySR independently.\n- That formula is the geometric mean of a proved lower bound and a proved upper bound. The sandwich `degeneracy + 1 ≤ optimum ≤ bandwidth + 1` holds on all 6,376 instances, forces the optimum on 2,823 where the two coincide, and where they differ the optimum sits at the midpoint on median in every size band, tracking sparsity rather than size.\n- None of it is a bound. The geometric mean is below the optimum on 1,495 instances and above on 600, and worse than the solver's bound at 61 to 134 customers. The one clean lower bound in it is dominated by the contraction degeneracy the solver already computes, so nothing goes to the bound work.\n\n**Next iteration** should take item 06, where iteration 6 left `learning/bound_gap.py` and its tests committed with a table run but no report section. Section 5 suggests starting its classifier from the degree coefficient of variation and separator size."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":642,"cache_read_input_tokens":181006,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":642,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":742,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"12577c41-7101-4638-b007-8765a211c262","uuid":"e52ba4ed-1af6-44c7-9a64-23d5e7b1c673","timestamp":"2026-09-25T20:23:33.978Z","request_id":"req_011CfQnK8ZsZUkrhmTCoLu3P"}
